  ('no_reservations', 2, 7, 'Japan', 'Osaka', 'Osaka', 'Japan', 34.693738, 135.502165, 'Anthony Bourdain''s Japanese adventure begins in Osaka at an underground bar devoted to the hardcore fans of the local baseball team, the Hanshin Tigers. Then he goes to the Kiso Valley for some relaxation.', '2006-05-08'),
  ('no_reservations', 2, 8, 'US/Mexico Border', 'Del Rio', 'Del Rio', 'USA', 29.370886, -100.895867, 'Tony visits Piedras Negras, Mexico, and border towns in Texas, where he sees the influences that the countries have had on each other. He also visits the Mexican restaurant credited with inventing nachos.', '2006-05-22'),
