  ('no_reservations', 5, 1, 'Mexico', 'Puebla', 'Puebla', 'Mexico', 19.04144, -98.206273, 'Tony travels to Mexico with Carlos, the Mexican executive chef of Les Halles, and the two visit Puebla, Carlos''s home town, and Mexico City. Tony eats Mexican foods like tortillas and roast pork and drinks pulque, an alcoholic beverage. He also attends a lucha libre school.', '2009-01-05'),
  ('no_reservations', 5, 1, 'Mexico', 'Mexico City', 'Mexico City', 'Mexico', 19.432608, -99.133208, 'Tony travels to Mexico with Carlos, the Mexican executive chef of Les Halles, and the two visit Puebla, Carlos''s home town, and Mexico City. Tony eats Mexican foods like tortillas and roast pork and drinks pulque, an alcoholic beverage. He also attends a lucha libre school.', '2009-01-05'),
  ('no_reservations', 5, 2, 'Venice', 'Venice', 'Venice', 'Italy', 45.440847, 12.315515, 'Tony goes in search of the less-touristy side of Venice, Italy, and meets locals and enjoys deep-fried crabs, baccalà and boiled calves'' heads.', '2009-01-12'),
  ('no_reservations', 5, 3, 'Washington, D.C.', 'Washington', 'Washington', 'USA', 38.907192, -77.036871, 'Tony visits Washington, D.C. and explores the diversity of its culinary options, including Irish, Mexican and Ethiopian food, as well as local landmark Ben''s Chili Bowl. He visits the International Spy Museum and practices one espionage technique, the dead drop. He then meets up with renown chef and restauranteur José Andrés for a tour of a Penn Quarter market and Andrés famed minibar.', '2009-01-19'),
  ('no_reservations', 5, 4, 'Azores', 'Azores', 'Azores', 'Portugal', 37.741249, -25.675594, 'After years of working alongside Azorean Portuguese immigrants in his early cooking career in New England, Tony travels to the Portuguese islands of the Azores. There, he visits a boiling geyser, and island hops to find out how the history, the region, and the food, all shaped and molded, the people with Azorean heritage of New England.', '2009-01-26'),
  ('no_reservations', 5, 5, 'Chicago', 'Chicago', 'Chicago', 'USA', 41.878114, -87.629798, 'Tony visits Chicago and samples local favorites like sausages, Chicago-style hot dog, and Burt Katz''s deep-dish pizza, as well as upscale dining. He also enjoys a giant Three Little Piggies sandwich with radio personality Mancow Muller.', '2009-02-02'),
  ('no_reservations', 5, 6, 'Food Porn', 'Hanoi', 'Hanoi', 'Vietnam', 21.0277644, 105.8341598, NULL, NULL),
  ('no_reservations', 5, 7, 'Philippines', 'Manila', 'Manila', 'Philippines', 14.599512, 120.984219, 'Tony visits Manila, Pampanga, and Cebu in the Philippines, traveling around with one of the runners-up of his FANatic contest, Augusto Elefano, to figure out just who are the Filipino people. After tasting Cebu''s famous Lechon, he considered it as the best pig ever.', '2009-02-16'),
  ('no_reservations', 5, 7, 'Philippines', 'Pampanga', 'Pampanga', 'Philippines', 15.079409, 120.619989, 'Tony visits Manila, Pampanga, and Cebu in the Philippines, traveling around with one of the runners-up of his FANatic contest, Augusto Elefano, to figure out just who are the Filipino people. After tasting Cebu''s famous Lechon, he considered it as the best pig ever.', '2009-02-16'),
  ('no_reservations', 5, 7, 'Philippines', 'Cebu', 'Cebu', 'Philippines', 10.315699, 123.885437, 'Tony visits Manila, Pampanga, and Cebu in the Philippines, traveling around with one of the runners-up of his FANatic contest, Augusto Elefano, to figure out just who are the Filipino people. After tasting Cebu''s famous Lechon, he considered it as the best pig ever.', '2009-02-16'),
  ('no_reservations', 5, 8, 'Disappearing Manhattan', 'Manhattan, New York', 'Manhattan', 'USA', 40.78306, -73.971249, NULL, NULL),
  ('no_reservations', 5, 9, 'Sri Lanka', 'Colombo', 'Colombo', 'Sri Lanka', 6.927079, 79.861243, 'Tony visits Colombo, Sri Lanka, samples the local food, and discusses the aftermath of the Sri Lankan Civil War and the 2004 tsunami.', '2009-03-02'),
  ('no_reservations', 5, 10, 'Vietnam: There''s No Place Like Home', 'Ho Chi Minh City', 'Ho Chi Minh City', 'Vietnam', 10.823099, 106.629664, 'Tony visits Vietnam, accompanied by his former boss, Les Halles owner Philippe Lajaunie. He is there to pay his respects to the family of Madame Ngoc, an old friend and restaurateur whose kindness and warmth touched Tony during his past visits. He visits the countryside, street markets and newly upscale areas of Ho Chi Minh City. At the end of the episode, he considers moving there.', '2009-03-09'),
  ('no_reservations', 5, 10, 'Vietnam: There''s No Place Like Home', 'Hội An', 'Hội An', 'Vietnam', 15.880058, 108.338047, 'Tony visits Vietnam, accompanied by his former boss, Les Halles owner Philippe Lajaunie. He is there to pay his respects to the family of Madame Ngoc, an old friend and restaurateur whose kindness and warmth touched Tony during his past visits. He visits the countryside, street markets and newly upscale areas of Ho Chi Minh City. At the end of the episode, he considers moving there.', '2009-03-09'),
  ('no_reservations', 5, 11, 'Chile', 'Santiago', 'Santiago', 'Chile', -33.44889, -70.669265, 'Tony visits Santiago and Patagonia in Chile. He attends a Chilean rodeo event and enjoys sopaipillas and beef braised in wine.', '2009-07-13'),
  ('no_reservations', 5, 11, 'Chile', 'Patagonia', 'Patagonia', 'Chile', -41.810147, -68.906269, NULL, NULL),
  ('no_reservations', 5, 12, 'Australia', 'Melbourne', 'Melbourne', 'Australia', -37.813628, 144.963058, 'Tony visits Melbourne, Australia, and samples food from the city''s diverse ethnic communities as well as at high-end restaurants. He also learns how to play Trugo.', '2009-07-20'),
  ('no_reservations', 5, 13, 'Rust Belt', 'Baltimore', 'Baltimore', 'USA', 39.290385, -76.612189, 'Tony visits the Rust Belt cities of Baltimore; Detroit, and Buffalo, New York, accompanied by Zamir Gotta. In Baltimore they meet with several of the cast members of the television show The Wire. In Buffalo they meet one of the other runners-up of the FANatic contest, Nelson Starr, and see his rock band perform. Zamir is discovered to have become a celebrity in the US in his own right, as a result of his previous No Reservations appearances.', '2009-07-27'),
  ('no_reservations', 5, 13, 'Rust Belt', 'Detroit', 'Detroit', 'USA', 42.331427, -83.045754, 'Tony visits the Rust Belt cities of Baltimore; Detroit, and Buffalo, New York, accompanied by Zamir Gotta. In Baltimore they meet with several of the cast members of the television show The Wire. In Buffalo they meet one of the other runners-up of the FANatic contest, Nelson Starr, and see his rock band perform. Zamir is discovered to have become a celebrity in the US in his own right, as a result of his previous No Reservations appearances.', '2009-07-27'),
  ('no_reservations', 5, 13, 'Rust Belt', 'Buffalo', 'Buffalo', 'USA', 42.886447, -78.878369, 'Tony visits the Rust Belt cities of Baltimore; Detroit, and Buffalo, New York, accompanied by Zamir Gotta. In Baltimore they meet with several of the cast members of the television show The Wire. In Buffalo they meet one of the other runners-up of the FANatic contest, Nelson Starr, and see his rock band perform. Zamir is discovered to have become a celebrity in the US in his own right, as a result of his previous No Reservations appearances.', '2009-07-27'),
  ('no_reservations', 5, 14, 'Down on the Street', 'New York City', 'New York City', 'USA', 40.7127753, -74.0059728, NULL, NULL),
  ('no_reservations', 5, 15, 'San Francisco', 'San Francisco', 'San Francisco', 'USA', 37.774929, -122.419416, 'Tony''s adventures takes him to the city of San Francisco, a city of districts and contradictions. So paying an homage to Steve McQueen''s iconic 1968 film Bullitt; Tony takes his rented Ford Mustang through the streets of San Francisco, from Fisherman''s Wharf, to Haight-Ashbury, to Chinatown, and across the bridge into Oakland, California. Tony dines with poet August Kleinzahler, and then off to chef Chris Cosentino''s restaurant for an offal tasting.', '2009-08-10'),
  ('no_reservations', 5, 16, 'Thailand', 'Bangkok', 'Bangkok', 'Thailand', 13.756331, 100.501765, 'Tony travels to Thailand and catches the beginning of the 2009 political unrest there. He also enjoys street food in Bangkok and explores Phuket. Later, Tony meets up with another runner-up of the FANatic contest, Eric Rivera, who is training for his Muay Thai fight.', '2009-08-17'),
  ('no_reservations', 5, 16, 'Thailand', 'Phuket', 'Phuket', 'Thailand', 7.951933, 98.338088, 'Tony travels to Thailand and catches the beginning of the 2009 political unrest there. He also enjoys street food in Bangkok and explores Phuket. Later, Tony meets up with another runner-up of the FANatic contest, Eric Rivera, who is training for his Muay Thai fight.', '2009-08-17'),
  ('no_reservations', 5, 17, 'Montana', 'Livingston', 'Livingston', 'USA', 45.661411, -110.559956, 'Tony travels to the state of Montana in the United States, where he visits a ranch and learns the struggles of being a rancher. He eats local specialties like beef, pasty, trout, and buffalo. Tony gets an understanding of why fly fishing is so addictive and meets with writer and local legend Jim Harrison, and artist Russell Chatham.', '2009-08-24'),
