  ('no_reservations', 7, 3, 'Nicaragua', 'Esteli', 'Esteli', 'Nicaragua', 13.085114, -86.36302, 'Tony visits Nicaragua to sample the cuisine, and in the process discovers the determination necessary to live in modern-day Nicaragua.', '2011-03-14'),
  ('no_reservations', 7, 4, 'Vienna', 'Vienna', 'Vienna', 'Austria', 48.208174, 16.373819, 'Tony visits wintery Vienna, Austria, visits Christmas markets, goes hunting suited like an aristocrat, eats sphincter and has, surprisingly, an overall good time. Tony finds out who Krampus is.', '2011-03-21'),
  ('no_reservations', 7, 5, 'Ozarks', 'West Plains', 'West Plains', 'USA', 36.728115, -91.852371, 'Tony visits West Plains, Missouri, backdrop of the book and film Winter''s Bone, and eats at Fred and Red''s. There, Tony explores the Ozark region and samples local specialties such as raccoon, venison and squirrel pot pie. He also goes fishing with novelist Daniel Woodrell, who breaks his shoulder on film.', '2011-03-28'),
  ('no_reservations', 7, 6, 'Brazil (the Amazon)', 'Belém', 'Belém', 'Brazil', -1.455729, -48.490179, 'Tony visits the city of Belém and the Amazon Rainforest in search of the undiscovered parts of Brazilian and more specifically Amazonian cuisine.', '2011-04-11'),
  ('no_reservations', 7, 7, 'Boston', 'Boston', 'Boston', 'USA', 42.360082, -71.05888, 'Tony visits the South Boston section of Boston, the neighborhood known as Southie, accompanied by guitarist Mike Ruffino of The Unband. They enjoy the local cuisine and bars and meet with local celebrities like columnist and talk-show host Howie Carr.', '2011-04-18'),
  ('no_reservations', 7, 8, 'Japan: Hokkaido', 'Sapporo', 'Sapporo', 'Japan', 43.062096, 141.354376, 'Weeks before the March 2011 quake, Tony visits Hokkaido, Japan. In Sapporo, he tries Hokkaido style ramen, waikanae crab, and Uni-ikura Don (salmon roe & sea urchin over rice). He visits with the indigenous people of Hokkaido, the Ainu. Tony ends his trip dining at a ryokan enjoying a formal robatayaki. In the international edition, viewers saw Tony visit the Sapporo Beer Garden for the “Genghis Khan” which is a specialty of Hokkaido.', '2011-04-25'),
  ('no_reservations', 7, 9, 'Cuba', 'Havana', 'Havana', 'Cuba', 23.113592, -82.366596, 'Tony travels to Cuba in the search of the island''s heart and soul where beauty abounds in the people, the food and the architecture and streets that are riddled with cars from before the revolution.', '2011-07-11'),
  ('no_reservations', 7, 10, 'Macau', 'Macau', 'Macau', 'China', 22.198745, 113.543873, 'Tony visits Macau, a former Portuguese colony south of Hong Kong now known as the Vegas of Asia, and tries his hand at some casino games. He also visits the Macau Tower bungee jump, the largest in the world, and takes the ultimate plunge.', '2011-07-18'),
  ('no_reservations', 7, 11, 'Naples', 'Naples', 'Naples', 'Italy', 40.851775, 14.268124, 'Tony travels to Naples, Italy, considered to be the root of Italian-American cuisine, to find out the differences and similarities between the original and its American counterpart.', '2011-07-25'),
